  m_Name: MultistageCentrifugalPumpData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: Multistage Centrifugal Pump
  engineDescription: 'A Multistage Centrifugal Pump is a dynamic fluid-handling device
    used to transport liquids at high pressures by passing the fluid through multiple
    impellers arranged in series within a single pump casing. It operates by converting
    the mechanical energy supplied by a motor into hydraulic energy, with each impeller
    progressively increasing the fluid pressure. Its main components include the
    pump casing, multiple impellers, diffusers, shaft, bearings, mechanical seals,
    suction and discharge nozzles, and coupling. During operation, liquid enters
    through the suction inlet and flows sequentially through each impeller stage,
    where its pressure is increased before being discharged at the outlet. The diffusers
    help convert the fluid''s velocity into pressure, improving the pump''s overall
    efficiency.


    Multistage centrifugal pumps are widely used in water supply
    systems, boiler feed applications, irrigation, power plants, mining, chemical
    processing, reverse osmosis systems, and high-rise building water distribution
    due to their ability to deliver high pressure with smooth and continuous flow.'
  engineCategory: Engineering
